Rule 2 explicitly states these rules **SHALL NOT APPLY** to:
- **(a)** **Railway servants** *(now governed by Railway Services (Implementation of NPS) Rules, 2025 — G.S.R. 735(E) dt. 01.10.2025)*;
- **(b)** Persons in **casual and daily rated employment**;
- **(c)** Persons **paid from contingencies**;
- **(d)** Members of the **All India Services** *(now governed by AIS (Implementation of NPS) Rules, 2026 — G.S.R. 307(E) dt. 22.04.2026)*;
- **(e)** Persons **locally recruited** for services in diplomatic, consular or other Indian establishments in **foreign countries**;
- **(f)** Persons **employed on contract**;
- **(g)** Persons whose terms and conditions of service are regulated by or under the **Constitution or any other law** for the time being in force;
- **(h)** Persons to whom the **CCS (Pension) Rules, 1972 [now 2021]** apply in accordance with any **special or general order** issued by the Government.

⚠️ EXAM TRAP / PROVISO ALERT: Probationers appointed substantively against regular posts ARE covered (see Rule 6(6)), whereas contract, casual, daily-rated, contingency-paid, Railway, and AIS officers are excluded under Rule 2(a)–(h).

- **Eligibility & Notice [Rule 12(1)]:** Anytime after completing **20 years' regular service**, by giving notice of **not less than 3 months in writing** to the **Appointing Authority**.
- **PROVISO — 3 Excluded Categories (including Scientist / Technical Expert):** Rule 12 **shall NOT apply** to a Subscriber who is:
  1. **(i)** On assignments under the **Indian Technical and Economic Cooperation (ITEC) Programme** of the Ministry of External Affairs and other aid programmes;
  2. **(ii)** **Posted abroad** in foreign-based offices of the Ministries or Departments;
  3. **(iii)** On a **specific contract assignment to a foreign Government**, **UNLESS**, after having been transferred to India, he has **resumed charge of the post in India AND served for a period of NOT LESS THAN ONE YEAR**!

⚠️ EXAM TRAP / PROVISO ALERT: Notice two ultra-specific exam traps: (1) Rule 12 uses '20 years REGULAR service' (compare CCS Pension Rule 43 '20 years qualifying service'); (2) Under Proviso (iii), after foreign-govt contract assignment, he MUST resume charge in India AND serve at least 1 YEAR before giving VRS notice!

1. **(a) Permanent Status:** The person concerned **was NOT a temporary Government servant** at the time of acceptance of his resignation;
2. **(b) Compelling Reasons & Material Change:** Resignation was tendered for **compelling reasons** NOT involving any reflection on his **integrity, efficiency, or conduct**, AND withdrawal request is due to a **material change in circumstances** which originally compelled him to resign;
3. **(c) Proper Intervening Conduct:** Conduct during the intervening period (between effective date of resignation and withdrawal request) was **in no way improper**;
4. **(d) 90-Day Ceiling on Absence:** Period of absence from duty between the **date resignation became effective** and the **date he is allowed to resume duty** is **NOT MORE THAN 90 DAYS**;
5. **(e) Availability of Post:** The **vacated post or any other comparable post** is available.

⚠️ EXAM TRAP / PROVISO ALERT: Look closely at TWO traps in Rule 14(3): (1) Clause (a) BARS temporary Government servants from withdrawing accepted resignation under this rule; (2) Clause (d) measures 90 days up to the date ALLOWED TO RESUME DUTY (not merely date of application — unless relaxed under Rule 28 with MoPPGP concurrence)!

- **Pre-Joining Application Exception:** **YES!** If a candidate had applied for another Government post **before** joining his first Government post, and **intimated that pending application at the time of joining**, resignation subsequently tendered to join that post **IS treated as Technical Resignation** (*'with proper permission'* under Rule 14(2))!
- **Consequences under Rule 14(2):**
  1. Continues with the **SAME PRAN** (if new Central/State Govt dept has NPS) and is **deemed an NPS member from initial joining date**;
  2. Past regular service counts towards **20-year VRS [Rule 12(1) Expl. (a)]** AND **Retirement/Death Gratuity** *(without requiring transfer of NPS corpus)*;
  3. **Lien Retention (Permanent Employees):** Retained in parent post for **2 years** (extendable up to **3 years** in exceptional cases where employee could not be confirmed in new post).

⚠️ EXAM TRAP / PROVISO ALERT: If an employee applied AFTER joining Govt service WITHOUT forwarding through proper channel / obtaining NOC, resignation is NON-TECHNICAL [Rule 14(1)] — forfeiting past service for gratuity & triggering 90-day 20:80 premature exit!

In **Form 3** [Rule 16(7)], the Medical Board / Civil Surgeon certifies:
1. Whether the Subscriber is **completely and permanently incapacitated for further service of any kind** in the Department to which he belongs (in consequence of specified disease/accident);
2. **OR** whether his incapacity is less than complete/permanent and he is **fit for further service of a less laborious character**;
3. Whether the incapacity **does NOT appear to have been caused by irregular or intemperate habits**; AND
4. His **age** according to his own statement (`... years`) and **by appearance** (`about ... years`).

⚠️ EXAM TRAP / PROVISO ALERT: Notice the classic clause inside Form 3: 'his incapacity does/does not appear to me/us to have been caused by irregular or intemperate habits', plus recording BOTH 'age by own statement' and 'age by appearance'!

**1. Inside `Form 4-A` (3 Asterisked Exit Paragraphs — ALL get Superannuation 60:40 Exit):**
- *Option 1:* Due for retirement on **superannuation** on `[date]` [Rule 11];
- *Option 2:* Notice for **voluntary retirement** accepted under **Rule 12** OR **FR 56(k)** OR **DoPT SVRS**;
- *Option 3:* Order for retirement issued by competent authority under **FR 56(j)** OR **DoPT SVRS** [Rule 13].

**2. Inside `Form 4-B` (Deemed Retirement on Absorption in AB/PSU OR Technical Resignation — 3 Scenarios):**
- *Scenario A (NPS exists in new AB/PSU / Govt Dept):* Subscriber **shall continue with SAME PRAN** in new organisation and **shall NOT receive any benefit at the time of absorption** [1st Proviso to R. 15(1) / R. 14(2)];
- *Scenario B (NPS does NOT exist in new AB/PSU & Subscriber opts to exit):* Process release of **superannuation-level terminal benefits** [R. 15(1) / 1st Proviso to R. 14(2)];
- *Scenario C (NPS does NOT exist & Subscriber opts to continue PRAN):* Continue **same PRAN as a non-Government subscriber** [2nd Proviso to R. 15(1) / R. 14(2)].

⚠️ EXAM TRAP / PROVISO ALERT: Many candidates forget that FR 56(k) is explicitly printed inside Form 4-A, and Technical Resignation is explicitly processed via Form 4-B alongside PSU/AB Absorption!
